        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "49acb803-5508-3c19-b46c-7d1115d364ff",
                "word": "infixe",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a1d0e8fb-586e-4fca-8073-814254d6c113",
                        "entry_id": "49acb803-5508-3c19-b46c-7d1115d364ff",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "infixes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa5444f0-d12e-3223-80a6-9f51c8d23e2d",
                        "entry_id": "49acb803-5508-3c19-b46c-7d1115d364ff",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Affixe qui s’insère à l’intérieur d’un radical et qui en modifie le sens ou la fonction."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "841d8ddc-e9e2-483b-86e7-03e08a3661a2",
                                "sense_id": "fa5444f0-d12e-3223-80a6-9f51c8d23e2d",
                                "text": "Les infixes sont communs dans les langues austronésiennes et austro-asiatiques. Par exemple, en tagalog, une forme grammaticale similaire à la voix active est formée en ajoutant l’infixe -um- près du début d’un verbe. Le tagalog a emprunté à l’anglais le mot graduate comme verbe, ce qui donne la forme dérivée grumaduate."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8001f393-6c24-477a-9876-85faa312b8c6",
                                "sense_id": "fa5444f0-d12e-3223-80a6-9f51c8d23e2d",
                                "text": "Plus haut, nous avons utilisé le terme général d’affixe pour désigner les morphèmes qui, ajoutés à la racine, servent à former un thème nominal ou verbal. Ce terme d’affixe recouvre les préfixes (antéposés à la racine), les infixes (insérés dans la racine) et les suffixes (postposés à la racine)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "49d6bf15-381f-46f7-9655-95b8c24f6f46",
                                "sense_id": "fa5444f0-d12e-3223-80a6-9f51c8d23e2d",
                                "text": "Il n’y a pas d’infixes en espéranto."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "90185ce2-6cef-4470-89e0-21001e3fcc2c",
                                "sense_id": "fa5444f0-d12e-3223-80a6-9f51c8d23e2d",
                                "text": "Enfin, en javanais on va intercaler un infixe (le plus souvent du type -av- ou -ag-) entre la voyelle et la consonne de chaque syllabe du mot: beau donne baveau, parler donne pavarlaver, gros donne gravos, citron donne savitravon, etc."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae5f5d01-cf8e-49fe-81e6-d235a37d4413",
                                "sense_id": "fa5444f0-d12e-3223-80a6-9f51c8d23e2d",
                                "text": "Quant au « conditionnel » marcherais, marcherais, marcherait, marcherions, marcheriez, marcheraient, l’infixe -r- du futur (marcherai, marcheras, marchera, marcherons, marcherez, marcheront) et la désinence -ais, -ais, -ait, -ions, -iez, -aient de l’« imparfait » (marchais, marchais, marchait, marchions, marchiez, marchaient) le rattachent sans l’ombre d’une hésitation à l’indicatif."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6cf0aa04-da7d-4510-91ff-e2e23bcc5c27",
                        "source_entry_id": "49acb803-5508-3c19-b46c-7d1115d364ff",
                        "source_sense_id": "fa5444f0-d12e-3223-80a6-9f51c8d23e2d",
                        "target_lang_word": "Infix",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Infix",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe6a77dc-79f1-3611-a0e4-cd75ac76d6b6",
                                        "entry_id": "0127b429-f54f-3318-8fff-6a69817d17dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Affix, also ein grammatisches Morphem, das in einen Wortstamm eingeschoben wird"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "special"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dee2f0f5-7f08-42ae-a4b3-68f20c5a04d0",
                                                "sense_id": "fe6a77dc-79f1-3611-a0e4-cd75ac76d6b6",
                                                "text": "„Als aber die semitischen Akkader von den nichtsemitischen Sumerern deren Keilschrift übernahmen, mußten sie sie ihrer eigenen flektierenden Sprache anpassen, in der auch die Wurzel der Wörter Veränderungen durch Vokalwechsel und Infixe erfährt.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e92d4d2-9503-4fe2-b47b-0a5f3d71579b",
                                                "sense_id": "fe6a77dc-79f1-3611-a0e4-cd75ac76d6b6",
                                                "text": "„Dieser Konjunktiv-Präsens wird gebildet mit /s-/, einem Infix -ij- und den üblichen Allomorphen für Person/Numerus (Sekundärendungen).“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f438df8-1111-4ae3-a9d9-d00c7cf80b18",
                                                "sense_id": "fe6a77dc-79f1-3611-a0e4-cd75ac76d6b6",
                                                "text": "„Außerdem gibt es noch das in das Grundwort eingeschobene Infix (von lat. infigere ‚hineinheften'). Im modernen Deutsch gibt es keine Infigierung in dem Sinne, dass ein Affix in einen Stamm eingefügt wird.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b947928c-1a39-42ec-aa52-10362a66ae13",
                                                "sense_id": "fe6a77dc-79f1-3611-a0e4-cd75ac76d6b6",
                                                "text": "„Bevor ich mich weiter grammatikalisch mit den untrennbaren Verben beschäftige, habe ich das Bedürfnis, gesellschaftlich über den Begriff »Präfix« und dessen Geschwister Suffix, Zirkumfix, Interfix, Infix und Suprafix zu sprechen. Ihr Überbegriff heißt tatsächlich »Affix«.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e5285f65-a768-36b3-8d7a-35c4b6b8dee1",
                                        "entry_id": "0127b429-f54f-3318-8fff-6a69817d17dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "in der Wortmitte stehendes Morphem, das auch anders interpretiert werden kann, zum Beispiel als Präfigierung in einem zusammengesetzten Wort"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Morphologie",
                                            "Deutsch"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd04e69a-0699-446c-9844-afbf4fe4fb77",
                                                "sense_id": "e5285f65-a768-36b3-8d7a-35c4b6b8dee1",
                                                "text": "Im Deutschen kann man die Wortbestandteile ›-ge-‹ (z.B. in „ein-ge-schoben“) und ›-zu-‹ (z.B. in „ein-zu-schieben“) als Infixe betrachten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c21108a-343a-4728-8f9f-dfefbfe17dcb",
                                                "sense_id": "e5285f65-a768-36b3-8d7a-35c4b6b8dee1",
                                                "text": "Im Deutschen ist zum Beispiel ›-ig-‹ ein Infix, mit dem Verben wie reinigen, begnadigen, befehligen, tätigen und heiligen gebildet werden."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5cffc1a0-a727-4fa7-99c9-2570fb437c2f",
                        "source_entry_id": "49acb803-5508-3c19-b46c-7d1115d364ff",
                        "source_sense_id": "fa5444f0-d12e-3223-80a6-9f51c8d23e2d",
                        "target_lang_word": "infix",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "infix",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b382a8bd-591b-3213-8857-e544f068bbe6",
                                        "entry_id": "4863f05b-1198-3703-b85d-ebe18866305a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To set; to fasten or fix by piercing or thrusting in."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57004628-8bef-4fcf-b311-b813d558eed5",
                                                "sense_id": "b382a8bd-591b-3213-8857-e544f068bbe6",
                                                "text": "to infix a sting, spear, or dart"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6569e6e6-d3a8-48ec-bdb4-67f469b538f1",
                                                "sense_id": "b382a8bd-591b-3213-8857-e544f068bbe6",
                                                "text": "[…] in her eye I find\nA wonder, or a wondrous miracle,\nThe shadow of myself form’d in her eye:\nWhich being but the shadow of your son,\nBecomes a sun and makes your son a shadow:\nI do protest I never loved myself\nTill now infixed I beheld myself\nDrawn in the flattering table of her eye."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16e08f1a-1771-41f5-8618-b94ca5457423",
                                                "sense_id": "b382a8bd-591b-3213-8857-e544f068bbe6",
                                                "text": "The fatal Dart a ready Passage found,\nAnd deep within his Heart infix’d the Wound:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc8714bf-dd00-48cf-bee9-5b61af3b86dc",
                                                "sense_id": "b382a8bd-591b-3213-8857-e544f068bbe6",
                                                "text": "Consider that innumerable race of insects, which either are bred on the body of each animal, or flying about infix their stings in him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4e6cdb4-f441-47df-abb8-366ba7fc1ab5",
                                                "sense_id": "b382a8bd-591b-3213-8857-e544f068bbe6",
                                                "text": "Gnawed within and scorched without, with the infixed, unrelenting fangs of some incurable idea; such an one, could he be found, would seem the very man to dart his iron and lift his lance against the most appalling of all brutes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37dc200e-9687-3fb3-b15f-f46626784d28",
                                        "entry_id": "4863f05b-1198-3703-b85d-ebe18866305a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To instill."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d701347a-b2d9-34ac-b420-f9ee06aa957d",
                                        "entry_id": "4863f05b-1198-3703-b85d-ebe18866305a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To insert a morpheme inside an existing word."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "infix",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7699e90-fb0d-38d2-b705-d7032170dee0",
                                        "entry_id": "54159b4a-1577-329f-ae1c-c8abdd951076",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An affix inserted inside a root, such as -ma- in English edumacation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2439f32b-66e8-4376-9e91-b5cbdfcc7684",
                                                "sense_id": "c7699e90-fb0d-38d2-b705-d7032170dee0",
                                                "text": "I am not pleased with one or two of the noun cases (they are too similar to others) and I want to change the way that the Focus category (see Section 3.5 of the grammar) is manifested (using word-order instead of an infix or other phonological marker). All in all, the language is structured almost exactly as I wanted."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f98027d-52c0-3fb4-944c-53b8fc99d3ee",
                                        "entry_id": "54159b4a-1577-329f-ae1c-c8abdd951076",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A prefix that is not at the beginning of a word, such as the con- of reconcile, or a suffix that is not at the end of a word, such as the -al of nationality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ea449e5-d2a6-4c9c-8099-a1ce8f00594b",
                                                "sense_id": "0f98027d-52c0-3fb4-944c-53b8fc99d3ee",
                                                "text": "The infix position contains (pronominal) object markers, showing agreement with the object(s), which might be one or more noun phrases following the verb, or a foregoing or previously mentioned object marking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31530b73-e84e-48d8-a8c6-703cea689f73",
                                                "sense_id": "0f98027d-52c0-3fb4-944c-53b8fc99d3ee",
                                                "text": "[…] but the second example contravenes all the rules, as the negative infix should NEVER precede any Set 2 affix present in the complex."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "550df33f-1215-4773-a4bc-9586a0729233",
                                                "sense_id": "0f98027d-52c0-3fb4-944c-53b8fc99d3ee",
                                                "text": "[…] at least in languages, like Swahili, which exhibit morphologically different tense/aspect infixes in affirmative and negative clauses[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3afab9e8-3d6a-4285-ae56-fffaea67da61",
                                                "sense_id": "0f98027d-52c0-3fb4-944c-53b8fc99d3ee",
                                                "text": "The morpheme in question is the reflexive prefix ('infix' in the traditional Bantu terminology)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0303e925-bfce-383d-9935-3fc20a5f2846",
                                        "entry_id": "54159b4a-1577-329f-ae1c-c8abdd951076",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A prefix that always occurs in the position immediately before the verb root, and which may in turn be preceded by other prefixes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "adad8128-0cbc-3073-92a1-e3488f5b9f1c",
                                        "entry_id": "54159b4a-1577-329f-ae1c-c8abdd951076",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of interfix."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "proscribed"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
